commit 74ced7ef382ec6c558b9c0b2db793017b1120043
Author: Claude <<redacted>>
Date:   Sat Oct 31 17:48:18 2026 +0000

    Finish a bag from its page

    A "Finish bag" button on the bag page (/coffee/{bag_id}) posts to
    /api/bags/{bag_id}/finish through the outbox. The store appends a new bags
    record under the same bag_id with finished_on set, the way a retraction is a
    new shot record: nothing is deleted or rewritten, and a resend writes nothing.
    The finished bag leaves Today, Switch coffee and the Log shot bag picker
    (they already skip finished bags) and stays in Coffees with its shots. Only
    the bag's owner can finish it; a day past tomorrow (UTC) is refused.

    Tests: the appended record and untouched lake files, the resend, the screens
    it leaves and the ones it stays on, per-user access, and a browser step
    online and offline.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <<redacted>>

